 "finding": "Put each line on the base the filings name and the model's final forecast year moves by a net SR 41.9 million of cost, which is -0.047 points of margin and -0.30% of the central. The offsets run BOTH ways and that is the finding: the levy and the licence fee fall against a group that grows faster than the Saudi segment they are charged on, while maintenance and subscriber-acquisition costs rise against it, and the two nearly cancel. The blended construction is not hiding a mix effect here \u2014 which is worth knowing precisely because the same test on another name in this book found one worth seventeen per cent."
